  "assumption_status": {
    "economics": "Scenario procurement rates and engineering allowances, not quotes or validated forecasts. Low launch prices require sustained high flight rate. No automatic productivity reduction is inferred from inflation.",
    "source": "Bennu measurements illustrate possible chemistry only; mining targets must be ordinary, independently surveyed and cleared. Water yield, extractability and energetically accessible inventory are assumptions.",
    "engineering": "Chemical rockets, modular mineral processing, solar power and cryogenic storage use known physical mechanisms. Autonomous maintenance, industrial scale, large pressure materials and GW beaming require qualification.",
    "renewal": "Additional physical replacement account: roads 40 years, other bulk 80, metals 50, 95 percent end-to-end recovered mass. This adds missing supplier throughput without rewriting earlier U maintenance accounts.",
    "startup": "Eight-year qualification/source bootstrap, five-year linear ramp, 20 equivalent years of stock delivery, then two-year final commissioning. Parallel site qualification assumed; no completion in 2041.",
    "propellant": "Near-stoichiometric water-derived H2/O2 avoids an indefinite oxygen-surplus inventory. 430 s at mixture near 8 is a design assumption, with 450 and 390 s bounds; chamber cooling and reusable life need qualification. Air oxygen is taken from the same electrolysis stream, making lander mixture slightly hydrogen-rich. Earth launch is a purchased methalox service with a separate gross resource screen.",
    "local_fleet_fabrication": "Separate design comparison: 70 percent of tug structural mass made from source metals after a 5 percent Earth-built seed, giving 66.5 percent locally made across the fleet; dry-to-payload ratio increases from 0.10 to 0.12. Earth supplies engines, electronics, specialty joints and alloyants. Aggregate 8 percent recoverable-metal grade and 60 percent recovery are unqualified source assumptions. No pressure-composite or semiconductor self-replication is inferred."
  },
